# Reading Azgaar's map (W2a): what a hand-made export in Azgaar's shape holds, and files that aren't one.

# Its two-line summary counts its rivers, settlements, routes and points of interest (W6a), and its
# cultures, religions and states (W6d), and ends with its fingerprint; an assert compares one line,
# so the snapshot checks it: 2 cultures, 3 religions and 2 states, each placeholder and removed one
# skipped.
world source crates/content/tests/fixtures/azgaar/tiny.json

# A Full export has cultures, religions and states (W6d); one without them isn't one.
assert world source crates/content/tests/fixtures/azgaar/no-peoples.json == error: this isn't a Full export: it has no pack.cultures; export the Full JSON from Azgaar

assert world source crates/content/tests/fixtures/maps/hand-made.map == error: cannot read crates/content/tests/fixtures/maps/hand-made.map: stream did not contain valid UTF-8
assert world source == error: world needs the form: world info <file>, world source <file>, world suggestions <map>, world tile <map> <x>,<y>, world dismiss <map> <id> [<id>…], world restore <map> <id> [<id>…], or world import <export> <map> [--region <x>,<y>,<width>,<height>] [--scale <n>] [--seed <n>] [--detail <strength>] [--wavelength <pixels>] [--octaves <n>] [--shallows <metres>] [--specks <tiles>] [--levels <points>] [--level-specks <tiles>] [--foliage <scale>] [--tree-spacing <tiles>] [--shrub-spacing <tiles>] [--grass-spacing <tiles>]
